{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"releasable-cankerous-hammerkop","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\nOn origin/main 38f8587f65d (2026-10-30), running these together with -n 4 fails 22 tests in tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_once.py:\n\npytest -q -n 4 tests/unit/reconciler/state tests/unit/reconciler/test_lock_steal.py tests/unit/reconciler/test_lock_orphan_local_ref.py tests/unit/test_last_pass_backoff_jitter_paediatric.py tests/unit/test_raw_git_write_lint.py tests/scripts/graph/test_repair_pause_ownership.py tests/interfaces/store tests/interfaces/facades tests/scripts/test_canary_status_refs_heldout.py tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate\n\n15 fail with BackendEnvError 'empty Jira Cloud read scope: the configured project (jira.project / JIRA_PROJECT) is unset' and 7 with ValueError 'inbound fetch requires a valid jira.project key ... got '''. The same tests pass when tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate runs with only tests/unit/reconciler/state and tests/interfaces/store + facades in a different grouping, and CI's gating cell is green, so the outcome depends on which tests share a worker. Reproduced twice on the same host (once with the S3 lock change applied, once on unmodified main).\n\n## Hypotheses\nA test in the co-scheduled set mutates process-wide Jira config (JIRA_PROJECT env, a cached rebar config, or a module-level project setting) without restoring it; or test_reconcile_once depends on config another test happens to set first. Unproven.\n\n## Plan\n1. Bisect the co-scheduled files with -p no:randomly -n 0 to find the first test after which test_reconcile_once fails.\n2. Identify the leaked state and fix the leak at its source (or make test_reconcile_once set its own project explicitly if it is relying on leaked state).\n3. Add a regression check that runs the polluting test before test_reconcile_once.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The command above passes on main.\n- [ ] The polluting test and the leaked state are named on this ticket.\n- [ ] A regression test fails before the fix and passes after.","id":"81da-a1b4-bf29-4ad2","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_reconcile_once fails when run in one session with interfaces/store and interfaces/facades"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793391888008841001,"uuid":"9afa6533-877e-4c49-b77a-d30059675e4f"}